From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pear <pear@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2001 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [mp] fix: a store's GPU blocks are held until it ends

After LMCache pull request #4955, "fix(mp): preserve and reload KV across preemption"
(https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/pull/4955), at its revision 83d9e57a2cc7b81c21a08fc66207452c5612b88f, ported onto
the commit of UPSTREAM.

In multiprocess mode a non-lazy STORE reads a request's GPU blocks after the forward pass that wrote them, and vLLM
may free those blocks before the copy is done: when it preempts the request, when align-mode Mamba drops a state
block the request has moved past (vLLM 0.34 does so every step, and once more when the request finishes, before it
calls the connector), or when the worker reports a finished request's in-flight stores as done because the server's
heartbeat lapsed. A freed block can go to another request and be overwritten, and the first request's hashes then
store the other request's KV or recurrent state; a later prefix hit continues from it. LMCache pull request #5248
(9a7b6050) waits for in-flight stores before the forward of a step with a preemption, but only up to the
message-queue timeout and for no other free; #5938 (752e01fd) delays a finished request's free only while a store of
it is scheduled, after vLLM has already dropped the Mamba blocks; #5886 (30dc05fb) pins only the boundary-state
blocks of unfull-chunk stores. Each STORE now holds a reference to every block it reads, from the step that schedules
it until every worker reports it terminal.

What the port takes and changes:
- The pull request's store lifetime in the connector, the metadata and the adapter, and its tests
  (tests/v1/test_mp_store_lifetime.py, the operation-level tests of tests/v1/test_vllm_mp_adapter.py), on
  v0.5.8rc1's API: packed token ids (lmcache.v1.common.token_codec), the transfer context's submit_store without
  instance_id, and no KV events on the worker: #6122 moved them to the scheduler, so a STORE keeps no events of its
  own and the worker metadata carries STORE results only.
- The pull request's reload of a request resumed after a preemption is left out, with its
  tests/v1/test_mp_preemption_loading.py: #5248 removed the same early return of get_num_new_matched_tokens. So are
  its return annotations and reformatting of code it does not otherwise change.
- The operation-level paths of submit_store_request and get_finished are the pull request's, in
  _submit_store_operation and _get_finished_with_store_operations, so that the request-level bodies, which lazy
  offload and vLLM's built-in fallback connector still use, stay as v0.5.8rc1 has them; the pull request's error for
  get_finished under lazy offload is left out. The operation path polls retrieves as v0.5.8rc1's request-level path
  does (_poll_transfer; a failed retrieve also goes into _failed_request_ids). A STORE operation whose query fails
  keeps its blocks; one whose result fails is a failed terminal.
- unregister_kv_caches (#6358) also waits for the operation-level STOREs before the engine releases the KV caches.
- request_finished no longer delays a non-lazy request's free, since its STOREs hold their own blocks. #5938's
  store_scheduled flag and its hand-over of delayed requests to the workers stay as v0.5.8rc1 has them; the non-lazy
  path no longer delays any request through them.
- The unfull-chunk STOREs of #5886 are pinned like every other STORE: the boundary-state block vLLM offers is one of
  the STORE's block IDs. The per-request pin (_pinned_boundary_state_blocks, released on a finished_sending report,
  which the operation path never makes) is removed.
- update_connector_output requires the GPU block pool only for a report with terminal operations.
- The pull request's names that are bare adjectives or participles are nouns, or booleans that ask a question
  (operation_store_lifetime is tracks_store_operations, succeeded is_failed, pinned pinned_operation and the like), its
  new functions have one-sentence docstrings, and a terminal STORE's result waits the adapter's mq_timeout, not 60 s.
- The adapter's default stays request-level, so v0.5.8rc1's adapter tests keep testing that path; the pull request's
  adapter tests run on an adapter built with tracks_store_operations=True (the operation_adapter fixture). Its
  non-writer rank is made through the is_kv_writer property, which #6125 decides per KV group, and a new test checks
  that unregistering the KV caches waits for an operation-level STORE.
- tests/v1/test_mp_connector_kv_roles.py asserts the per-STORE references instead of v0.5.8rc1's delayed free of a
  finished request with a scheduled store, checks that ranks without a STORE's future still report it terminal, and
  binds the block pool in its MultiConnector and block-allocation tests as vLLM's scheduler does.
  tests/v1/test_mp_connector_unfull_chunk.py checks the per-STORE pin of the boundary-state block, also across a
  preemption, and tests/v1/lazy_offload/test_mp_connector.py's eager keepalive follows the pinned STOREs.
  tests/v1/lazy_offload/test_worker_adapter.py's adapter, built without its constructor, sets the request-level
  default of tracks_store_operations, which submit_store_request now reads.
- tests/v1/test_mp_store_lifetime.py also runs vLLM's own BlockPool: a block vLLM frees while a STORE reads it stays
  out of the free queue until every rank reports the STORE terminal.
